# VA-LAYER EDIT FREEZE — TU5 RE-BASE IN PROGRESS

**Declared:** 2026-07-12 by the TU5 re-base coordinator (approved by project owner).
**Steering doc:** docs/plans/roadmap-2026-07-12.md  ·  memory: project-tu5-rebase-decision

## FROZEN until the atomic TU5 flip lands (do NOT edit in main):
- config/45410914/splits.txt
- config/45410914/symbols.txt
- config/45410914/config.yml   (touching it re-runs the split/renamer)
- scripts/target_symbol_map.json

## Why
The project's build target is being re-based from base/TU0 to TU5 (v0.0.5.1).
All of the above regenerate together off `base_to_tu5_map.full.json` and land in
ONE atomic commit. Any in-flight main-tree edit to these files will be clobbered
by the flip (and vice-versa, your matches would be lost).

## What you CAN still do
- src/ C++ matching work (name-keyed, survives the flip untouched)
- work in your own worktree
- anything not touching the four files above

## Landing / lifting
P2–P4 run in `.claude/worktrees/tu5-migrate`. Flip gate: matched >= 15,768
(guaranteed floor; worst-case 15,595 — every drop enumerated in the roadmap).
This marker is DELETED by the flip commit. If it is still here, the freeze is live.
